9-23T18:17:10Z","git_url":"git://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF","homepage":"http://agentfield.ai/","size":196153,"stargazers_count":116,"watchers_count":116,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":14,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":141,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-fleet","agent-harness","agentfield","agentic-coding","ai","ai-coding","cli-agent","coding-agent","coding-agents","coding-assistant","coding-cli","coding-harness","developer-tools","harness","harness-engineering","llm","open-models","open-source-models","software-factory","terminal-agent"],"visibility":"public","forks":14,"open_issues":141,"watchers":116,"default_branch":"dev","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls/1409","html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1409","diff_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1409.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1409.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Skills (#1277), on top of #1410. It is based on `santos/dev2`, which already has Santosh's skills work: skills from other tools read in place, `/skill`, `use_skill`, and skills chosen per message. #1396 is still landing there. When #1410 merges and `santos/dev2` is deleted, GitHub retargets this pull request to `dev`.\n\n**Draft. Do not merge before #1410.**\n\n## What is in it now\n\n- **`.opencode/skills` and `.goose/skills` are read too**, under the project and the home directory. #1277's day-one list names both. They rank after the other six folders, so an earlier folder's copy of a name wins and the later copy stays in the result, marked shadowed.\n- A change entry.\n\n## Checked\n\n- `make pr-ready BASE=origin/santos/dev2`: exit 0.\n- **Real binary, real model (`deepseek-v4-flash`), throwaway home, driven in tmux.** Four skills were placed:\n  - with the `npx skills` CLI, patched with a codeaf entry (#1399): one in the project (`add -a codeaf`, lands in `.agents/skills`) and one global (`add -g -a codeaf`, lands in `~/.agents/skills`)\n  - by hand: one in the project's `.opencode/skills` and one in the home's `.goose/skills`\n\n  All four were listed in the `/skill` picker. Each was used by the model on its own, and each answer carried that skill's unique marker line. The global one went through `use_skill get`.\n- **On `santos/dev2` as it stands, attaching from `/skill` does not work in the real binary.** Every row says `memory is off, so this cannot be attached` even with `memory.enabled` on. The picker asserts `SkillFacts` on the surface's memory seam, but the launch hands it the `v3Brain` adapter (`cmd/codeaf/chatv3.go`), which does not forward that method. The picker test passes only because its fake memory has the method. #1396 moves that read onto the session. I built #1396's head with this pull request's commit cherry-picked (it applies cleanly and `internal/skills` tests pass). There the warning is gone, `enter` attaches, and the turn shows `· skills · goose-honk, open-sesame, house-greeting`.\n\n## Still to do here\n\n- After #1396 lands in `santos/dev2`: rebase, and add OpenCode and Goose to its `skills-from-other-tools` manual page in the same commit.\n- #1277's plan items that #1410 does not have: per-skill slash commands, `/skill add` and `/skill remove` from a folder or a git URL, and a Skills tab. The plan's per-scope on/off conflicts with #1410's choice by meaning, and needs Santosh's call first. The sub-issues #1404–#1408 are being re-scoped as gaps against #1410.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1409/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1409/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]